{"duration_api_ms":204829,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c8fb79bd-afb1-4b1d-b588-85fdc58e74ee","total_cost_usd":0.145477,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11841,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24357,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":22470},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11841,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":10,"output_tokens":24357,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11841},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":24357,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11841,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.145477,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":22470,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"merged_document\": \"# BIP: 39\\n\\n## Abstract\\n\\nThis BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence—a group of easy to remember words—for the generation of deterministic UTOXs. It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into an ASCII seed. This seed can be later used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\\n\\n## Copyright\\n\\nThis BIP falls under the GPL License.\\n\\n## Motivation\\n\\nA mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet satoshis. The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\\n\\nThis guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated determinism with a human-readable transcription. It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\\n\\n## Generating the Mnemonic\\n\\nThe mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits. With more entropy, security is improved but the sentence length increases. The initial entropy length is referred to as ENT, and the allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\\n\\nFirst, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated. A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA-256 hash. This checksum is appended to the start of the initial entropy. Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 12 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist. Finally, these numbers are converted into words, and the joined words form the mnemonic sentence.\\n\\nThe following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words.\\n\\n```\\n| CS = ENT / 32\\n| MS = (ENT + CS) / 11\\n| \\n| |  ENT  | CS | ENT+CS |  MS  |\\n| +-------+----+--------+------+\\n| |  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\\n| |  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\\n| |  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\\n| |  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\\n| |  256  |  8 |   264  |  24  |\\n| ```\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039.mediawiki\",\n  \"decisions\": [],\n  \"dispositions\": [\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a3\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence—a group of easy to remember words—for the generation of deterministic UTOXs.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Changed 'letters' to 'words' for factual accuracy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a4\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into an ASCII seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Corrected grammar from 'a' to 'an' before vowel.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a12\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Corrected encoding error 'süeed' to 'seed'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b1\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"## Generating the Mnemonic\",\n      \"reason\": \"Fixed typo 'memonic' to 'Mnemonic' and capitalized heading.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b2\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Fixed typo 'demonic' to 'mnemonic' and corrected bit multiple.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b3\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"With more entropy, security is improved but the sentence length increases.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added comma for grammatical clarity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b4\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reconciled\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The initial entropy length is referred to as ENT, and the allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Combined with b5 to form one complete statement about ENT.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b5\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reconciled\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The initial entropy length is referred to as ENT, and the allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Combined with b4; corrected range from '1024-2048 byts' to '128-256 bits'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA-256 hash.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Corrected algorithm from 'SHA652' to 'SHA-256'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b10\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Finally, these numbers are converted into words, and the joined words form the mnemonic sentence.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Converted to passive voice for consistency.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"mismatch\": \"\",\n  \"additions\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence—a group of easy to remember words—for the generation of deterministic UTOXs.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"easy to remember letters\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"Mnemonics consist of words, not individual letters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"multiple of 23 bits\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP 39 entropy values (128–256 bits) are multiples of 32.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The initial entropy length is referred to as ENT, and the allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"1024-2048 byts\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP 39 valid ENT range is 128–256 bits, confirmed by table.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA-256 hash.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"SHA652\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"SHA652 is not a real algorithm; BIP 39 uses SHA-256.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"wallet süeed\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"Character encoding error; correct word is 'seed'.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":194595,"type":"result","duration_ms":204892,"uuid":"b9e7bd49-1533-4fbe-987b-30078c58aae1","ttft_stream_ms":989,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":990,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
